1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,865
Do you know how to intrude the lower incisors without changing their inclination?

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,905
It all depends on where the line of action of the force passes relative to the center of resistance.

3
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,969
If the force passes in front of it, the incisors tend to tip labially.

4
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:31,008
If the line of action passes through the center of resistance, we get predominantly bodily intrusion.

5
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:37,001
But what happens if we shift the line of action behind the center of resistance?

6
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:41,419
An opposite moment arises, promoting lingual tipping of the crowns.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,272
One cantilever. Three lines of action. Three different biomechanical effects.

8
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:57,494
That's why it's important to control not only the magnitude of the force, but also its point of application and direction.
